WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Thomas Ruyant, the defending IMOCA champion for the Route du Rhum, has withdrawn from the November start because he could not secure a major sponsor for his new foiling boat. This is Offshore North, Episode 6. Scott Shawyer is working to become the first Canadian to finish the Vendée Globe, the solo non-stop round the world race that begins in 2028. To the Canadian boat, as of the 2nd of September, Emira 4 was leaving Canada and heading back to Europe. That post is Scott Shawyer's own account of the summer training

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.040
on George and Bay. He described the biggest learning as understanding how the boat works system

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:41.680
by system. The list includes sales, rigging, foils, electrical systems, hydro generators, solar panels,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:47.020
and autopilot overlays. Scott noted that after more than 40 years sailing on Lake Huron,

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:53.760
the water conditions held few surprises. The boat itself did. On two heavy days, his triceps seized on

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.680
the grinder. He traces that to a shoulder injury and not drinking enough water with electrolytes.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:04.080
He added that he has still not sailed Emira for in open ocean waves and swell, and needs

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:04.880
to remain humble.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.320
The support team named includes Martin Amescuah, who have been with the boat for a long time.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:17.180
Gabi Bukau, Clovis Gautier, Gelina Bayat for rigging in systems, Alberto Zaccaria for electrical,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.300
computer and sensor systems, Alan Roberts for coaching on the exoset routing system and

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:25.520
autopilot overlays, and Nick Maloney as sailing coach.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.480
The boat was not among the 14 Imocha's that started the 48-hour azimuth in

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:35.000
Lorient on the 17th of September. The next confirmed milestone remains the

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.420
root newrum start on the 1st of November from St. Mallow. That will be Shawier's

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:44.220
first solo transatlantic on a foiling Imocha. Scott has sailed Lake Huron for

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:49.060
over 40 years, so the water was familiar but the boat systems were new. I'm

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:52.720
learning a similar lesson right now with the foils on my wingboard on Georgian Bay.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:58.100
way. Same physics, just smaller and slower. Out in the fleet, Lake Keep reported this

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.780
week that Thomas Ruyant will not start the root du-rum on the 1st of November. The defending

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.380
Imocha champion cited the failure to secure a major sponsor for his new foiling Imocha,

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:13.240
and the roughly 2.5 million euros required for the race and ongoing operations. The boat

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:18.680
launched on the 19th of June remains in storage in Lorient. Ruyant called the decision in

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:23.560
immensely disappointing. He noted that the race has a particular place in his history. Yet

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:28.860
he stated that his ambitions for the Imocha Circuit and the 2028 Bonday Globe remain unchanged,

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:35.340
with the energy even stronger. He had sought major backing for about 2.5 million euros to participate

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:41.340
competitively. The team needs 4 to 5 million euros per year until the Bonday Globe. Other skippers,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:47.010
including Armel Tripon and Maxime Sorrell, are also still seeking funding for the same start in

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:52.050
intense sponsorship market. The withdrawal leaves one fewer established name on the 26-boat

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:57.250
Imocha entry list for a race that already sits in a tight sponsorship market. Sailors

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:02.110
reported this week that Anthony Martian completed winter modifications on actual Ultim IV.

00:03:02.710 --> 00:03:07.590
Those changes included a taller mast at the Class Maximum height and a revised sail plan.

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:13.050
The work allows earlier takeoff, more mast bend, and the ability to flatten the main sail

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.510
further without reefing early.

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:20.530
Martian described the work as preparation for his primary 2026 objective, the Root-Durum

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:22.290
on the 32-meter trimoran.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.750
He noted that the new mast allows proactive adjustments that were not possible with

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.750
the previous wing mast.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:34.130
The sail inventory was adjusted accordingly, with main sail, J3 and J2 all at the same

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:34.790
sail area.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:40.090
The modifications illustrate how even established ultim teams continue to chase marginal gains

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:44.610
Things in a class where small differences in rig behavior can decide a solo Atlantic crossing.

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:46.350
Time for plain sailing.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:51.490
And Imocha campaigns annual operating budget typically runs between four and five million

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.430
year-olds once a new boat is in the water.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:59.230
That figure covers the boat itself, shore team, spares, travel, insurance, and the skipper

00:03:59.230 --> 00:03:59.670
salary.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:04.830
Most of it must be raised from title sponsors who treat the campaign as media exposure rather

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:05.590
than philanthropy.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:10.790
When a sponsored relationship ends or a new one cannot be closed in time, the boat stays

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:12.510
ashore even if it is ready to race.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:17.710
The Root-Duram entry list shows how quickly that arithmetic can remove a defending champion

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:18.570
from a start line.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:23.550
Ruyant had launched his new boat in June, but could not raise the necessary funds.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.590
A skipper must also complete at least one great two solo race on the boat they will race

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:34.150
in the Vondi Globe, finishing within twice the winner's time, and finish among the top 37

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:39.450
in the Imocha Globe Series Championship for a place in the 40-boat fleet, and the countdown.

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:45.290
783 days remain until the Bondi Globe start on the 12th of November, 2028.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:51.150
The campaign's next concrete milestone is the Root-Duram start on the 1st of November, 2026

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:56.370
from St. Mallow. That's Offshore North for this week. Every source is linked in the episode

